<p>If your dog ate wrapping paper, a small torn piece is usually not an emergency, but call your vet if a large amount, ribbon or string was eaten, or signs of trouble appear. Plain paper is mostly a blockage risk, not a poison; foil, ribbon and string raise the stakes. Do not induce vomiting or pull visible ribbon.</p>

