<h2>Signs of a Blockage After Eating Wrapping Paper</h2>
<p>Signs of an intestinal blockage include vomiting, not eating, belly pain, diarrhea, dehydration and lethargy, according to Cornell's Riney Canine Health Center and the Merck Veterinary Manual. Any of these after your dog ate wrapping paper, ribbon or cellophane need a vet visit, and some need an emergency vet right away.</p>

